; Static export surface of the `version.dll` proxy.
;
; This is the documented Win32 `version.dll` surface: 16 named exports, no
; ordinal-only exports. Every line is a PE export forwarder, so the proxy emits
; no forwarding code of its own - the Windows loader resolves each name straight
; into the real system module.
;
; The target is written as the System32 path, not as the bare module name. A
; bare `version.dll` forwarder resolves through the default search order, which
; finds the proxy itself in Steam's directory first and recurses forever; the
; qualified path can only mean the real module. In a 32-bit (WoW64) process the
; loader's file-system redirection turns the same string into
; `C:\Windows\SysWOW64\version.dll`, which is the right module there.
;
; A missing export is not a build error: the client keeps running, and the first
; Steam call into the missing name fails inside the loader. So the list has to
; be complete, and a client update that adds an export must be noticed. That is
; what `crates/host-windows/src/proxy.rs::plan()` is for: it reads the export
; directory of a real module and can regenerate this list on any machine, from
; the example `cargo run -p vapor-forge-host-windows --example proxy_plan --
; <module.dll> version.dll --emit-def`. Re-run it against the shipped
; `version.dll` if a build turns out to need one more export, then diff.
;
; GNU ld cannot express a path containing `\` in a forwarder (it splits the line
; on the backslash), so the path uses forward slashes. The Windows loader
; accepts them.
LIBRARY version.dll
EXPORTS
  GetFileVersionInfoA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoA
  GetFileVersionInfoW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoW
  GetFileVersionInfoExA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoExA
  GetFileVersionInfoExW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoExW
  GetFileVersionInfoSizeA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoSizeA
  GetFileVersionInfoSizeW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoSizeW
  GetFileVersionInfoSizeExA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoSizeExA
  GetFileVersionInfoSizeExW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.GetFileVersionInfoSizeExW
  VerFindFileA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerFindFileA
  VerFindFileW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerFindFileW
  VerInstallFileA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerInstallFileA
  VerInstallFileW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerInstallFileW
  VerLanguageNameA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerLanguageNameA
  VerLanguageNameW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerLanguageNameW
  VerQueryValueA=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerQueryValueA
  VerQueryValueW=C:/Windows/System32/version.dll.VerQueryValueW
